## Explanation

A user wants to access `www.foobar.com`.

The browser asks the DNS system for the IP address of `www.foobar.com`.
The domain `foobar.com` has a `www` record pointing to the server IP address `8.8.8.8`.

The browser then sends an HTTP request to the server. The server receives the request through the web server, Nginx.

Nginx handles the HTTP request. If the request is for dynamic content, Nginx forwards it to the application server.

The application server runs the backend logic of the website. It uses the application files, also called the code base.

If data is needed, the application communicates with the MySQL database.

Finally, the response is sent back to the user's browser.

## Specific Questions

### What is a server?

A server is a physical or virtual machine that provides services or resources to other computers, called clients.

### What is the role of the domain name?

The domain name makes the website easier to access for humans. Instead of typing an IP address, users can type `www.foobar.com`.

### What type of DNS record is `www` in `www.foobar.com`?

`www` is usually an A record when it points directly to an IPv4 address.

In this case:

`www.foobar.com -> 8.8.8.8`

### What is the role of the web server?

The web server receives HTTP requests from users and sends HTTP responses back.

In this infrastructure, Nginx is the web server.

### What is the role of the application server?

The application server executes the application logic. It processes dynamic requests, runs backend code, and communicates with the database when needed.

### What is the role of the database?

The database stores and organizes data such as users, posts, products, orders, or any dynamic information used by the website.

### What is the server using to communicate with the user's computer?

The server communicates with the user's computer using the HTTP protocol over TCP/IP.

## Issues With This Infrastructure

### SPOF

This infrastructure has a Single Point of Failure because everything is on one server.

If the server goes down, the whole website becomes unavailable.

### Downtime During Maintenance

When deploying new code or restarting Nginx or the application server, the website may become unavailable.

### Cannot Scale

If too much traffic arrives, the single server may become overloaded. Since there is only one server, the infrastructure cannot handle large traffic easily.